  rank 3: [doc1_bfs.txt#0] score=0.000  &quot;Breadth-first search explores a graph level by level, using a FIFO queue to hold the frontier of unvisited nodes. It guarantees the shortest path in terms of number of edges when every edge has the same cost.&quot;
  --- assembled context (truncated) ---
  Answer the question using ONLY the context below. Cite the source tag you used.
  
  ...
